  "label": "Text: 'is a labor of love'",
  "description": "This text completes the phrase 'some people say religion is a labor of love,' which is a common cultural trope used to describe religious devotion as a self-sacrificing, heartfelt, and often difficult commitment. The meme uses this phrase to frame the contrast with the image of a man being physically restrained while carrying a cross, implying that religious practice can be coercive or burdensome — thus mocking the idea of it being a 'labor of love.'",
